3194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442613 1069 "q-127379" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442613 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442613 1071 "The equations of a curve $r(t)$ and its corresponding unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at an arbitrary point are given below. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at the point $P(2,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ) \\\\ T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨2,\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442613 1072 #uuid "f08885d9-557e-5e55-b967-a7cb452a9e2a" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442613 1074 "First, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(2,\\frac{1}{2})$ on the given curve. We know that:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩ \\\\ ⟨2t,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}2t=2 \\\\ \\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value also satisfies the other equation. Therefore, $P(2,\\frac{1}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$ \n\nNow, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨2,\\,t⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}})⟨2,\\,t⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(⟨2,\\,t⟩) \\\\  & =-\\frac{t}{{({t}^{2}+4)}^{3/2}}⟨2,\\,t⟩+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+4}}⟨0,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{({t}^{2}+4)}^{3/2}}(-t⟨2,t⟩+({t}^{2}+4)⟨0,1⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{({t}^{2}+4)}^{3/2}}⟨-2t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  \\\\ {T}^{′}(1) & =\\frac{1}{{((1)^{2}+4)}^{3/2}}⟨-2(1),\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{5}^{3/2}}⟨-2,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}‖⟨-1,2⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the principal normal vector to the curve at the point where $t=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(1) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(1)}{‖{T}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2⟩}{(\\frac{2}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that when we find the scalar product of $T$ and $N$ at the point where $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1)\\cdot N(1) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,1⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(⟨2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2⟩) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(2(-1)+1(2)) \\\\  & =0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442606 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1069 "q-358780" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1071 "$$\nT(t)=\\frac{1}{13}(-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+12\\,k).\n$$\n\nThe unit tangent vector to a curve at an arbitrary point is given above. Find the principal normal vector to that curve at an arbitrary point on the curve.\n\n$N(t)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j$" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1072 #uuid "f357a402-4ed9-5871-9002-ee2ada823334" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true] [17592186442614 1074 "First, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{13}(-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+12\\,k)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12)\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we find the magnitude of ${T}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{5}{13}‖\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{5}{13}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)}{\\frac{5}{13}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534884 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00435226-3a19-5eb9-bdc3-0cc889991ef8" 17592186442563 "answer-02e39ea1-4cba-57a5-ab90-7a89782cb8d0" 17592186442564 "answer-09429f0b-5a31-576e-b53c-7a9c9089a259" 17592186442565 "answer-18b10125-03d9-569f-b489-2af1cd51651f" 17592186442566 "answer-283cc10c-c7dc-5d42-98bb-ff049bacb22b" 17592186442567 "answer-28cf7792-7abc-5ff9-b607-d63d93877d58" 17592186442568 "answer-34323a95-3364-5d8b-ae6b-9b380e0bf2c9" 17592186442569 "answer-37ad2308-55f9-592a-86af-f156397fae09" 17592186442570 "answer-39d23c9a-dade-5d1b-902c-eabbc6bdf7de" 17592186442571 "answer-3d439e47-3587-59b8-90e6-26a8e6ad90ab" 17592186442572 "answer-496f3c19-e7a7-5744-b55a-b824329dc81c" 17592186442573 "answer-4b50b45b-e31f-500e-9496-cc48c7886b21" 17592186442574 "answer-4df4322e-2ca8-59b0-b25f-d74e9d345855" 17592186442575 "answer-512116d3-97dd-54be-bc16-10567d150eb8" 17592186442576 "answer-524146c4-7e77-5f6d-af6c-ffd660ac28d6" 17592186442577 "answer-54e8dd13-f4d3-59cf-aea8-647ea53c3240" 17592186442578 "answer-625e5e39-ae98-52ef-bfcc-de3e0bace052" 17592186442579 "answer-63b699bf-e6d8-5ef0-9f70-0ede7e9e9edb" 17592186442580 "answer-6f1effa6-46d0-5a74-afd6-d9566c6fab86" 17592186442581 "answer-77fd4f80-1bca-57c5-b06d-9f6931a1ae23" 17592186442582 "answer-85f9b3c0-76af-5d80-92a4-5941254da04b" 17592186442583 "answ